    "content": "As of March 2026, over 10 million pounds of Trader Joe's frozen fried rice and chicken shu mai are recalled due to potential contamination with hard plastic or glass pieces. Affected products, produced by Ajinomoto Foods, were sold nationwide (except in 7 states) and include Vegetable Fried Rice, Chicken Fried Rice, and others, with specific best-by dates in 2026 and 2027. Recalled Products and Details: Vegetable Fried Rice: Best by dates 02/28/2026 to 11/19/2026. Chicken Fried Rice: Best by dates 03/04/2026 to 02/10/2027. Japanese Style Fried Rice: Best by dates 02/28/2026 to 11/14/2026. Chicken Shu Mai: Best by dates 03/13/2026 to 10/23/2026. What to Do:Consumers should check their freezers, immediately stop using these products, and return them to any Trader Joe’s for a full refund. Recall Scope:The recall was initiated due to numerous consumer complaints regarding foreign objects, identified as glass, ranging from 1-3 cm in length, which likely originated from carrots in the products. The recall is considered a significant safety hazard, with the FDA listing it under a serious, potential health consequence classification.",
